== an invalid KOSHCONF does not stop startup:
kosh
rc=0
== a Bash name points at its koshconf name:
-c:1:14: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Unknown option 'pipefail'.
note: 'pipefail' is the Bash name of 'posix.interpreter.pipeline_fails_on_any_stage'.
-c:1:37: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Unknown option 'extglob'.
note: 'extglob' is the Bash name of 'bash.interpreter.glob_extended_patterns'.
== enumeration values read naturally:
-c:1:31: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Invalid value 'ed' for 'editor.base_mode', expected 'emacs' or 'vi'.
-c:2:56: error: Builtin `koshconf`: Invalid value 'true' for 'completion.add_space_after_completed_word', expected 'off', 'on', or 'on-excluding-trailing-slash'.
== --persist skips a byte order mark:
 357 273 277 b a s h . i n t e r p r e
 t e r . g l o b _ i n c l u d e
 s _ d o t f i l e s = o n \n
== --persist keeps CRLF line ends:
 m o o d = b a s h \r \n e d i t o
 r . a u t o _ c l o s e _ b r a
 c k e t s _ a n d _ q u o t e s
 = o n \r \n e d i t o r . h i s t
 o r y . m a x _ e n t r i e s =
 9 \r \n
== --persist ends an unterminated last line with the CRLF of the file:
 m o o d = b a s h \r \n e d i t o
 r . a u t o _ c l o s e _ b r a
 c k e t s _ a n d _ q u o t e s
 = o f f \r \n e d i t o r . h i s
 t o r y . m a x _ e n t r i e s
 = 9 \r \n
== --persist of the kosh mood drops the lines the mood fixes:
mood=kosh
editor.history.max_entries=9
startup-rc=0
== --persist fills a commented placeholder in place:
# Store history here.
editor.history.file_path=/tmp/h
mood=bash
== a missing configuration base reports the exact environment state:
-c:1:1: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The user configuration file cannot be located because XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset and HOME is unset.
-c:1:1: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The user configuration file cannot be located because XDG_CONFIG_HOME holds the relative path 'relative' and HOME is unset.
-c:1:1: error: Builtin `koshconf`: The user configuration file cannot be located because XDG_CONFIG_HOME is empty and HOME is unset.
